2. [x] bay 2's helm: services orders bay 1's `helm` line; helm.ps1 is bay 1's; uv in gear.yml
3. [x] crew.py/crew.ps1 keep each crew's state by its name (production keeps editing-bay-1); fcpm crew names this machine's crew
4. [x] helms.yml: editing-bay-2 holds wizard:model+up too; a reply's `job` picks the bay; no address -> waits
4b. [x] bay 2 follows main by itself (crew line `follow` every 15m): orders are merged commits
5. [ ] On FCPMEDIT2: start line (start-line URL until #406 merges), fcpm model install/pick, fcpm crew install, fcpm helm grant
6. [ ] Bay 2's address on Helm (10.209.1.x) -> helms.yml `at:`
7. [ ] /models/ page: choose the bay (sends `job`); MODEL_AT per bay
8. [ ] digitization's asks: answer from whichever bay serves the asked model (today FCPM_MODEL_AT, bay 1 only)
9. [ ] Network mode: ggml-rpc-server on bay 2 for bay 1's --rpc; no auth, so Helm-only rule, on only while tried
10. [ ] A LAN start: a bare machine starts from the origin, not GitHub. Needs an anonymous read path for
        public repos only (troves are private); the board's call (asked 2026-11-09)
10b. [ ] Keys before the machine: who admits a new bay's key to KEYHOLDERS without GitHub; the board's call
10c. [ ] One supervisor for every job a machine wears, so a second job needs no administrator
10d. [ ] fcpm origin (agreed 2026-11-09): bay key -> KEYHOLDERS PR -> fetch from origin.local, push to GitHub
